From 43b6638148dcbc8e3db98079835867021032aad1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <325961+iav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:54:01 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 03/20] rocket: DPU_SURFACE_ADD = Wout*Hout cells (drop RK3588
 magic *2)

Vendor librknnrt 1.5.2 computes DPU SURFACE_ADD (0x40c0) as the output
surface size in 16-byte cells, Wout*Hout (= output_surface_stride).
Mesa used Wout*Hout*2. For the reference conv2d 80x80x16->40x40x128 5x5 s2
this yields 0x6400 (vendor-exact) instead of 0xc800.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_task.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_task.c b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_task.c
index 5a910a97442..ffbade8eea3 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_task.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_task.c
@@ -145,7 +145,11 @@ fill_task(struct rkt_ml_subgraph *subgraph,
    else
       task->weights_kernels = align(operation->output_channels, 2);
 
-   task->surfaces_per_row = task->output_width * task->output_height * 2;
+   /* RK3568 (vendor librknnrt 1.5.2, RE 2026-08-20): DPU SURFACE_ADD is the
+    * output surface size in 16-byte cells = Wout * Hout, i.e. equal to
+    * output_surface_stride.  The previous *2 was an RK3588-era magic
+    * multiplier (elements-vs-cells mismatch). */
+   task->surfaces_per_row = task->output_width * task->output_height;
    if (operation->depthwise)
       task->surfaces_per_row *= 2;
 }
-- 
2.53.0


From 2ce088e21d6ea728a7fa19dadc63b252c46ca618 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <325961+iav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:55:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 04/20] rocket: CNA DMA line/surf stride in 16-byte cells
 (vendor formulas)

Vendor librknnrt 1.5.2: CNA_DMA_CON1 line_stride = Win and CNA_DMA_CON2
surf_stride = Win*Hin, both in FEATURE_ATOMIC_SIZE (16-byte) cells.
Mesa divided line_stride by 4 and used line*(Hin/4 - 1) for surf_stride.
