Subject: [PATCH 10/20] rocket/rk3568: fix CORE register map, add CMAC MISC_CFG
 and DPU_RDMA 0x5024

The vendor command stream extracted from any .rknn shows three things mesa
got wrong on RK3568:

- The CORE block map in registers.xml is one slot too high: it has a
  spurious MAC_GATING at 0x300c, so MISC_CFG/DATAOUT_SIZE_0/DATAOUT_SIZE_1
  all shifted up by four bytes.  Mesa was writing QD_EN into what the
  hardware reads as DATAOUT_SIZE_0, telling CORE its output was three
  pixels wide and one high.
- CMAC MISC_CFG at 0x200c was never written (QD_EN, plus DW_EN for
  depthwise).
- DPU_RDMA 0x5024 is absent from registers.xml and never written; the
  vendor puts output_channels - 1 there in every task, and without it the
  bias RDMA fetches nothing.

With these the pipeline completes for the first time on RK3568: the DPU
interrupt arrives, DT_WR is non-zero and the job no longer times out.
Numerical output is still wrong -- the DPU mode registers (DATA_FORMAT,
BS/BN configs, RDMA burst config) remain to be matched.

