All of these were read off the vendor command stream embedded in .rknn
model files, across 44 convolution tasks of mobilenet_v1 and 23 of
resnet18:

- CNA_DMA_CON0 is the constant 0x00171c07 on every geometry: both burst
  lengths are 7 and FETCH_PIXEL_LEN is 28, not input_width.
- CNA_CONV_CON2 FEATURE_GRAINS is weights_height + stride_y, one less than
  mesa emitted.  (The vendor raises it further when it schedules more than
  two output lines per CBUF pass, which mesa never does.)
- CNA_CBUF_CON1 carries the input width in its upper half.
- CNA_CONV_CON4 RGB_BYTELENGTH is written only in ARGB mode.
- CNA_CVT_CON0 keeps CVT_BYPASS clear on non-ARGB layers.
- DPU_DST_SURF_STRIDE is output_width * output_height / 2.

With these the reference 80x80x16 -> 40x40x128 conv completes without any
override, in 4.6 ms instead of a 500 ms timeout.

