From 5c1bfd4fa9e6792eb16280a196132ba8411d0754 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iav <iav@iav.lv>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 00:21:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 14/20] rocket/rk3568: CBUF banks are 64 KiB, and bands must
 not overshoot

Two sizing errors that made mesa split layers it did not need to split.

CBUF_BANK_SIZE was 32768.  The vendor command stream says otherwise: the
first convolution of mobilenet_v1 is 224 wide with seven data banks, and
the vendor splits it into bands of 127 and 98 input rows.  At 14 entries
per row that first band needs 128 slices, which only fits if a bank holds
256 entries of 256 bytes -- 64 KiB.  With half the real capacity mesa cut
the same layer into five bands, and cut layers that need no splitting at
all into two or three.

The band loop also handed each task every available CBUF slice, which
leaves a spare input row whenever the slice count is not congruent to the
kernel height modulo the stride: mesa fed CNA 128 rows where 63 output
rows consume (63 - 1) * 2 + 3 = 127.  The vendor carries exactly 127.

Single-layer tests at mobilenet_v1 shapes -- 1x1 at 112x112x32 to 64,
3x3 stride 2 at 112x112x32, depthwise 3x3 stride 1 and 2, plain 3x3 at
56x56x32, and the 80x80x16 to 40x40x128 reference -- now fit in one task
each and all complete.  Three of them needed two or three bands before
and timed out.

