From be39766243f54ddf85bdf43700b30367be8f8970 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <325961+iav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 20:00:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 17/20] rocket: RK3568 native 8-channel feature atomics end to
 end

The RK3568 NPU feature format is planar 8-channel surfaces with 8 bytes
per pixel (surface stride W*H*8), and every CNA/DPU stride register is
in 8-byte units -- half the RK3588 sizes mesa assumed.  Verified against
a live vendor capture of a 28x28x32 3x3 probe (input impulse at (3,14,0)
lands at byte (3*28+14)*8) and against all 51 mobilenet_v1 vendor tasks:

- input packing and output readback: planar 8-channel groups;
- DATA_ENTRIES = W * ceil(C/8) / 4 (32-byte CBUF entries, 8-ch atomics);
- CBUF is 8 banks of 32 KiB (1024 entries); data banks take the minimum,
  weights get the rest -- reproduces every vendor CBUF_CON0/CON1 value;
- band split offsets are rows * W * 8 bytes;
- weight layout for regular convolutions: 16-kernel groups, tap-major,
  32-channel input slices above the kernels (byte-exact vs vendor);
- per-tensor requant variant (BS MUL_BYPASS, OW from BS_OW_OP register,
  bias-only BRDMA stream) as the vendor emits for per-tensor models.

Full probe suite (identity, id64, d32, dic, dtap, c28, conv-56, pw-112,
dw-112, dw-s2, conv-s2-112, first-16ch) now matches TFLite CPU within
+/-1 LSB on uniform fills, row/column gradients, channel codes and a
mixed spatial-channel pattern.  Remaining known gap: the ARGB first
layer path (Cin=3), so whole-model mobilenet_v1 still diverges.
