From 96c6ea32da99c4c4ff9653e522805d842e6a72f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <325961+iav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 21:52:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] rocket: RK3568 depthwise 32-channel groups; keep
 oversized FC on CPU

Depthwise convolutions with more than 32 channels run as one task per
32-channel group, mirroring the vendor stream (mobilenet_v1 t6..t9:
full tasks for group 0, address-delta tasks for group 1):

- every band is duplicated per group; the group shifts the feature
  address by Win*Hin*32, the weight pointer (DCOMP_ADDR0) by KH*KW*32,
  the destination by Wout*Hout*32 and the BS stream by 32 channels;
- the depthwise weight buffer becomes [group][tap][32 channels] so the
  per-group weight offset lands on a group boundary;
- CBUF_CON0 WEIGHT_REUSE is dropped on the first task of each group --
  new group, new weights (this was the actual garbage source: group 1
  silently reused group 0 weights);
- entries_per_slice uses the 32-channel group size for band sizing,
  matching the vendor band heights.

Fully-connected-shaped convolutions whose weights exceed the 256 KiB
CBUF (the final 1024->1001 1x1) are reported unsupported until the
vendor fp16 FC mode is implemented; the conv path wedges on them.

Adds TEFLON_MIN_OPS (with TEFLON_MAX_OPS: delegate a window of plan
nodes) and RKT_MAXROWS (force extra bands) debug knobs.

mobilenet_v1 end to end on the NPU: 87 ms vs 117 ms CPU, zero job
timeouts, logit mean abs diff 0.11 (max ~48), 4 of top-5 classes match
the CPU reference.  The layer probe suite stays at max 1 LSB.
---
